  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OrPower Geothermal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The expected Project-level outcomes include improving the reliability of electricity and reducing reliance on imports by expanding baseload generation at a cost lower than the countrys average cost of service. Beyond such effects, the Project will improve the competitiveness of Kenyas power sector, by demonstrating the benefits of the public private risk sharing model for the development of further geothermal electricity generation. This can help the country to scale up reliable baseload in line with its Least Cost Power Development Plan (LCPDP).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment entails an IFC own account loan of up to $30 million and mobilization of up to $34.4 million through a Parallel Loan and the Managed Co-lending Portfolio Program (MCPP), to finance the construction and operation of the 35MW Orpower Twenty Two Limited (Geothermal) Project located in Menengai, Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
